From fcae90b60f0ef098c216f2fb528b63b77360febe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brandon Arrendondo <brandon.arrendondo@bissell.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 21:25:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] FT: Fix off-by-2 buffer bounds check in wpa_ft_process_rdie()

wpa_ft_process_rdie() bounds-checks the (Re)Association Response frame
element buffer with:

    if (end - pos < (int) sizeof(*rdie)) {
            ...
            return pos;
    }

which only verifies there is room for sizeof(*rdie) (the 4-byte RDIE
body). It then writes the 2-byte RIC Data EID/length header *before*
the RDIE body:

    *pos++ = WLAN_EID_RIC_DATA;
    *pos++ = sizeof(*rdie);
    rdie = (struct rsn_rdie *) pos;
    rdie->id = id;
    rdie->descr_count = 0;
    rdie->status_code = host_to_le16(WLAN_STATUS_SUCCESS);
    pos += sizeof(*rdie);

so the function actually needs 2 + sizeof(*rdie) bytes of room, but
only checked for sizeof(*rdie). With exactly sizeof(*rdie) bytes
left in the response buffer, the two header bytes fit but the
rdie->id/descr_count/status_code writes land 2 bytes past the end of
the buffer.

This could at least theoretically be reached while building the
(Re)Association Response frame to a station during an IEEE 802.11r fast
BSS transition, driven by RIC Data subelements the station included in
its own (Re)Association Request frame (wpa_sm_write_assoc_resp_ies() ->
wpa_ft_process_ric() -> wpa_ft_process_rdie()). Due to the extra buffer
room in (Re)Association Response frame generation, it is not clear
whether there is any realisitc way of reaching the buffer limit, though.

Include the header bytes in the bounds check to fix this check.

Signed-off-by: Brandon Arrendondo <brandon.arrendondo@bissell.com>
---
 src/ap/wpa_auth_ft.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/ap/wpa_auth_ft.c b/src/ap/wpa_auth_ft.c
index 76b14ddd35cc..172f3db40718 100644
--- a/src/ap/wpa_auth_ft.c
+++ b/src/ap/wpa_auth_ft.c
@@ -2416,7 +2416,7 @@ static u8 * wpa_ft_process_rdie(struct wpa_state_machine *sm,
 	wpa_hexdump(MSG_MSGDUMP, "FT: Resource descriptor IE(s)",
 		    ies, ies_len);
 
-	if (end - pos < (int) sizeof(*rdie)) {
+	if (end - pos < 2 + (int) sizeof(*rdie)) {
 		wpa_printf(MSG_ERROR, "FT: Not enough room for response RDIE");
 		return pos;
 	}
